{
  "app": "realworld",
  "derivedBy": "hand, from the application sources at the pinned commit",
  "method": [
    "Every screen is a route entry in app.routes.ts or profile.routes.ts that places a component on the primary outlet.",
    "Every navigation site is a routerLink attribute or binding, or a Router.navigate/navigateByUrl call, found by searching the sources; test and spec files are excluded.",
    "The screens a site fires from are the screens whose routed component renders, transitively through template element selectors, the component whose file holds the site. The shell (app.component) holds the router-outlet, so what it renders appears on every screen.",
    "A site inside a service is attributed to the screens from which the enclosing method can actually be called, found by searching for callers of that method, not to every component that injects the service.",
    "This file is the author's reading of the sources and is not independent of the author. It is recorded here so a reader can check it against the same sources rather than take it on trust.",
    "Its first version missed nine sites in the header, because the search that enumerated them discarded every line carrying routerLinkActive and the header writes both attributes on one anchor. They were found by the scorer, which reports sites the graph places and this file does not list; that check is the only one this file gets, and it earned its place immediately."
  ],
  "screens": [
    "/",
    "/tag/:tag",
    "/login",
    "/register",
    "/settings",
    "/profile/:username",
    "/profile/:username/favorites",
    "/editor",
    "/editor/:slug",
